  "id": "meritocracy",
  "term": "meritocracy",
  "definition": "Meritocracy is the idea that rewards and opportunities should go to people because of their ability and effort rather than unrelated personal factors. In psychology and education, it can also mean a person’s belief that success, especially academic success, mainly comes from effort and ability.",
